WEBVTT

00:00:04.718 --> 00:00:05.802
(grunts)

00:00:05.886 --> 00:00:07.095
(yells, grunts)

00:00:07.179 --> 00:00:08.347
(growls)

00:00:10.807 --> 00:00:12.100
(grunts)

00:00:13.977 --> 00:00:15.270
(gasps)

00:00:15.354 --> 00:00:17.230
-(panting)
-(growls)

00:00:18.565 --> 00:00:20.025
Whoa!

00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:22.986
Gotcha.

00:00:24.529 --> 00:00:26.114
Whoa.

00:00:29.618 --> 00:00:30.452
Hmm.

00:00:30.535 --> 00:00:31.370
(growls)

00:00:31.453 --> 00:00:32.287
(both grunt)

00:00:32.371 --> 00:00:33.497
Let go of me.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:35.207
Where do you think you're going?

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:36.249
Whoa.

00:00:38.418 --> 00:00:39.878
Switchback Cove.

00:00:40.545 --> 00:00:42.631
-It's the way home.
-(chatter in distance)

00:00:43.131 --> 00:00:44.216
DIEGO: Oh, no.

00:00:44.299 --> 00:00:45.675
GUTT: You call this a ship,

00:00:45.759 --> 00:00:47.511
-you miserable runts?
-(screams)

00:00:47.594 --> 00:00:49.471
Yeah, you little runts.
Get to work.

00:00:49.554 --> 00:00:52.557
GUTT: Faster, you worthless,
wormy sons of sorry excuses

00:00:53.183 --> 00:00:54.893
for shark bait weevils!

00:00:54.976 --> 00:00:56.436
-What did he say?
-I don't know.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:59.856
Now, get this chunk of ice
seaworthy by sundown,

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.359
or I will keelhaul
the lot of you.

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.569
-Hah!
-(crew screaming)

00:01:04.986 --> 00:01:06.029
MANNY:
So, what do you think?

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:09.491
Two words:
anger management. Ow!

00:01:09.574 --> 00:01:11.243
I'm talking about the current.

00:01:11.326 --> 00:01:13.787
Diego's right,
we found the way home.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:15.914
SID: Yeah, that's...

00:01:15.997 --> 00:01:17.374
that's great.

00:01:17.457 --> 00:01:18.875
Too bad we don't
have a ship.

00:01:18.959 --> 00:01:20.085
Sure, we do.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.295
It's right there.

00:01:22.379 --> 00:01:24.297
SHIRA: Well, that's
a flawless plan.

00:01:25.132 --> 00:01:28.135
You want to pirate
a pirate ship from pirates.

00:01:28.218 --> 00:01:31.096
It pains me to say this,
but our prisoner has a point.

00:01:31.179 --> 00:01:33.098
-Yeah, well...
-Guys, shh.

00:01:33.181 --> 00:01:35.767
(whispering):
The trees have ears.

00:01:35.851 --> 00:01:37.144
(low whispering)

00:01:38.562 --> 00:01:40.814
(chittering)

00:01:40.897 --> 00:01:43.275
(squeaking)

00:01:43.358 --> 00:01:46.027
(whispered chattering)

00:01:48.155 --> 00:01:48.989
(Gutt laughing)

00:01:49.072 --> 00:01:51.116
(crew screaming, whimpering)

00:01:51.741 --> 00:01:52.868
Wait a minute.

00:01:52.951 --> 00:01:54.828
Maybe we can help each other.

00:01:55.162 --> 00:01:56.413
(chatters)

00:01:56.496 --> 00:01:57.998
Hey, little fellas.

00:01:58.081 --> 00:01:59.082
Hey, come on out.

00:01:59.791 --> 00:02:00.876
MANNY: No, no, no, no, it's okay.

00:02:01.209 --> 00:02:02.169
We're not going to hurt you.

00:02:02.252 --> 00:02:03.086
(chattering)

00:02:04.588 --> 00:02:07.799
How about you and us
against the pirates? Huh?

00:02:10.552 --> 00:02:12.262
You got no idea
what I'm saying, do you?

00:02:12.345 --> 00:02:16.141
Okay, uh, ship, me want.

00:02:16.224 --> 00:02:17.976
Yeah, nice try, Jungle Jim.

00:02:18.059 --> 00:02:18.894
MANNY:
Oh, go ahead, make fun.

00:02:18.977 --> 00:02:20.103
Okay, he got it.

00:02:20.187 --> 00:02:21.897
(chattering)

00:02:22.272 --> 00:02:23.899
Oh, uh...

00:02:23.982 --> 00:02:25.233
(chattering)

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:26.818
Thank you.

00:02:26.902 --> 00:02:27.986
Uh, may I try?

00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:29.613
Yeah, knock yourself out.

00:02:29.696 --> 00:02:32.866
Okay, watch this.

00:02:32.949 --> 00:02:34.034
(clears throat)

00:02:34.117 --> 00:02:35.285
♪ Me, me, me, me, me. ♪

00:02:35.368 --> 00:02:37.370
Sick sloths sip broth,
sick sloths sip broth.

00:02:37.454 --> 00:02:38.997
(clears throat)

00:02:39.998 --> 00:02:42.667
Wuga, wuga, wuga, wuga.
Puda, puda, puda, puda.

00:02:42.751 --> 00:02:44.044
(spluttering)

00:02:45.086 --> 00:02:47.172
(squawks, splutters, growls)

00:02:47.255 --> 00:02:48.465
(all scream)

00:02:48.548 --> 00:02:49.841
(angry chattering)

00:02:49.925 --> 00:02:50.842
(hooting)

00:02:52.552 --> 00:02:54.012
Wiggy, wiggy, wiggy,
wiggy, wiggy.

00:02:54.095 --> 00:02:55.639
(grunts, yodels)

00:02:55.722 --> 00:02:56.806
(Sid grunting)

00:02:56.890 --> 00:02:58.391
(splutters) Ta-da.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.185
ALL: Oh.

00:03:00.268 --> 00:03:01.436
That, they got?

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.021
(whispered chattering)

00:03:03.104 --> 00:03:05.357
Hi-ya! Hah!

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.692
(rhythmic grunting)

00:03:07.776 --> 00:03:10.362
(all scream, grunt)

00:03:10.737 --> 00:03:11.988
Yep, they're in.

00:03:12.072 --> 00:03:13.323
Great. We'll free
your buddies,

00:03:13.406 --> 00:03:14.699
and we can all
work together

00:03:14.783 --> 00:03:16.493
to kick a little
pirate booty.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.037
-(all cheering)
-(Sid whooping)

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:30.215
(bird calling in distance)

00:03:35.011 --> 00:03:36.179
-(branch snapping)
-(growls)

00:03:36.555 --> 00:03:38.223
Easy, kitty. Water.

00:03:38.848 --> 00:03:40.058
You need it.

00:03:42.143 --> 00:03:43.436
SHIRA: I don't need
anything from you.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:44.521
Fine.

00:03:44.604 --> 00:03:46.523
Die of thirst.
That'll really show me.

00:03:46.606 --> 00:03:47.732
SHIRA: Wait.

00:03:48.066 --> 00:03:49.109
I'll take it.

00:03:49.859 --> 00:03:50.902
Thank you.

00:03:50.986 --> 00:03:52.654
You know, you have a way
of saying "thank you"

00:03:52.737 --> 00:03:55.031
that makes it sound
like "drop dead."

00:03:55.115 --> 00:03:56.992
-It's a gift.
-(sighs)

00:03:57.075 --> 00:03:59.035
Well, you're pretty soft
for a saber.

00:03:59.119 --> 00:03:59.953
Excuse me.

00:04:00.036 --> 00:04:01.454
I am not soft, okay?

00:04:01.538 --> 00:04:03.290
I happen to be a
remorseless assassin.

00:04:03.373 --> 00:04:05.041
Diego poo!

00:04:05.125 --> 00:04:07.085
Hey, I made you
another coral necklace.

00:04:07.168 --> 00:04:08.587
He keeps losing them.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:10.171
(giggling)

00:04:10.255 --> 00:04:11.798
(humming)

00:04:11.881 --> 00:04:13.592
Yeah, I think
I'm starting to get

00:04:13.675 --> 00:04:14.634
why you're not
in a pack.

00:04:14.718 --> 00:04:16.928
Listen, I chose to leave
my pack, all right?

00:04:17.012 --> 00:04:19.014
Congratulations,
warrior princess.

00:04:19.556 --> 00:04:20.599
So did I.

00:04:20.682 --> 00:04:22.225
-Really?
-What?

00:04:22.309 --> 00:04:25.186
Nothing. I just...
I know how hard that is.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:26.813
Walking away
from everything you know.

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:28.607
Oh, great.
What, are we going to braid

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:30.525
-each other's fur now?
-Funny.

00:04:30.859 --> 00:04:31.943
Really funny.

00:04:32.027 --> 00:04:33.612
Can I tell you the difference
between you and me?

00:04:33.695 --> 00:04:35.405
I wouldn't still be
wearing that necklace?

00:04:35.488 --> 00:04:36.656
Huh? Ugh.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:37.574
No.

00:04:37.657 --> 00:04:39.367
We both might have
wanted out of pack life,

00:04:39.451 --> 00:04:41.911
but at least I didn't trade
one pack for another.

00:04:41.995 --> 00:04:43.121
I got something more.

00:04:43.204 --> 00:04:45.123
Oh, yeah? What's that?

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:46.708
A herd.

00:04:46.791 --> 00:04:47.917
What's the difference?

00:04:48.001 --> 00:04:49.294
We have each other's backs.

00:04:49.377 --> 00:04:50.420
Gutt has my back.

00:04:50.754 --> 00:04:52.464
-I'm his first mate.
-Really?

00:04:52.547 --> 00:04:53.798
'Cause I don't see
Gutt sending out

00:04:53.882 --> 00:04:54.883
any search parties for you.

00:04:57.135 --> 00:04:58.470
You know, you won't beat him.

00:04:59.054 --> 00:05:00.722
Your big, furry friend
over there--

00:05:01.431 --> 00:05:03.141
he has no idea
what he's up against.

00:05:03.224 --> 00:05:05.644
Yeah, but neither does Gutt.

00:05:05.727 --> 00:05:08.355
Unwind the vines. Don't let go
until we're all on board.

00:05:08.438 --> 00:05:12.192
Okay, we need precision timing
from everyone to get that ship.

00:05:12.275 --> 00:05:13.985
Half-pint, you've got
your end covered, right?

00:05:14.819 --> 00:05:16.738
(fierce grunting)

00:05:17.864 --> 00:05:19.449
-(all grunt)
-(snarls)

00:05:19.532 --> 00:05:21.534
Going to take that as a yes. Diego?

00:05:21.618 --> 00:05:23.203
I'll free his little friends.

00:05:23.286 --> 00:05:24.412
-Sid and Granny?
-SID: Sir!

00:05:24.496 --> 00:05:26.456
-Untie the ship, sir!
-Right.

00:05:26.539 --> 00:05:27.832
Unwind the vines.

00:05:27.916 --> 00:05:29.626
Don't let go
until we're all on board.

00:05:29.709 --> 00:05:31.044
We're relying on you, Sid.

00:05:31.127 --> 00:05:32.462
-You got that?
-Oh, yes, sir.

00:05:32.545 --> 00:05:33.588
Totally focused, sir.

00:05:33.672 --> 00:05:35.423
Don't worry. It'll be easy

00:05:35.507 --> 00:05:37.801
since we don't have
to guard Shira anymore.

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:40.095
(all gasp)

00:05:42.472 --> 00:05:43.973
We need to move now.

00:05:44.057 --> 00:05:45.975
GUTT: Squint, batten down the hatches.

00:05:46.059 --> 00:05:48.269
-Raz, hoist the anchor.
-Aye.

00:05:48.353 --> 00:05:50.313
And, Gupta, fly the colors.

00:05:50.397 --> 00:05:52.107
Of course, Captain.
(giggles)

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:53.358
GUTT: We're setting sail

00:05:53.441 --> 00:05:55.110
for vengeance, lads.

00:05:55.193 --> 00:05:56.903
Ooh. I love vengeance.

00:05:56.986 --> 00:05:57.862
(laughing)

00:05:57.946 --> 00:05:58.780
Captain.

00:05:58.863 --> 00:05:59.906
Shira.

00:05:59.989 --> 00:06:02.492
Oh, what a relief.

00:06:02.575 --> 00:06:03.952
I thought we'd lost you.

00:06:04.035 --> 00:06:06.204
The mammoth-- he washed
ashore with me. He's...

00:06:06.287 --> 00:06:07.622
What? He's here?

00:06:08.206 --> 00:06:10.458
(grunts) Did you sink
your fangs into him?

00:06:10.542 --> 00:06:12.502
Did he beg for his life?

00:06:12.585 --> 00:06:14.671
No. The saber took me down.

00:06:14.754 --> 00:06:17.090
(growls) You're a failure.

00:06:17.632 --> 00:06:20.218
I need warriors,
and all I have

00:06:20.301 --> 00:06:22.679
are kitty cats
and bunny rabbits.

00:06:22.762 --> 00:06:25.098
Uh, and a seal
and a kangaroo. (laughs)

00:06:25.181 --> 00:06:26.349
(sighs)

00:06:26.433 --> 00:06:30.395
You take the saber down,
or you die trying.

00:06:30.729 --> 00:06:33.523
No excuses.

00:06:33.606 --> 00:06:34.816
Yes, Captain.

00:06:34.899 --> 00:06:36.651
-(Shira exhales)
-Mr. Squint.

00:06:36.735 --> 00:06:37.736
Aye, sir.

00:06:37.819 --> 00:06:39.904
You're first mate now.

00:06:39.988 --> 00:06:42.866
Yo-ho-ho and a bottle
of cool-with-me, Captain.

00:06:42.949 --> 00:06:44.409
Out of my way, saber.

00:06:44.492 --> 00:06:45.660
You answer to me now.

00:06:45.744 --> 00:06:47.746
Gutt, listen,
he's coming for the...

00:06:47.829 --> 00:06:49.038
-(horn blowing in distance)
-Hmm?

